    "show_share": true,
    "description": "When COVID-19 hit, doctoral students around the world carved their own ways to make progress on their degrees, within the confines of the pandemic. At the same time, educational institutes recognised the need to tailor their operations, to fit the new normal. Now that we have eased back into life, we must take stock of individual and collective experiences to study the impact of the crisis and chart a way forward.",
